  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We need to know in Udon if someone is using SDK2 or SKD3 avatars and also if they use FBT, e.g. to give them a station which doesn't break their avatar, or to not let them into a specific station and display a message instead. \nRight now, we can either make a station that fully works for SDK3 avatars or for SDK2 avatars. When it comes to FBT users, it get's even more complicated for certain use cases. There are also things that should work differently if the user has full body tracking, not related to stations at all.\n\"But what are you doing that breaks SDK2/3 avatars?\"\nWe e.g. import parts of the Avatar SDK3 into our SDK3 world unity project to override certain tracking by animation and to adjust the viewpoint. We do this because else the animation / viewpoint only works for SDK2 avatars. Using those components breaks SDK2 avatars. It also breaks some stuff on SDK3 when they exit, like finger tracking, or IK, but the user can at least manually reset their avatar to fix that.\n\"But wouldn't it be better to fix stations instead?\"\nWe are waiting for working stations since forever and a fix for them usually breaks with the next update. There are so many broken/unexpected behaviour things with stations that we should not wait until an update will fix all issues we are having on our weird use-cases. A lot of people do awesome stuff by using stations in unintended ways or want to tailor something to be used by FBT or a certain avatar version, not only limited to stations.\nNote: There is a guide regarding stations where the avatar version can branch in an animator. This is good, but does not cover any use case, especially if you need the information without or before having the user in a station. https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrc_station#sdk3-station-with-sdk2sdk3-avatar",
